WEBVTT

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:05.650
<i>Our opponent in the quarterfinals is 
the powerhouse that is Touto Boys.</i>

00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.150
<i>And their ace on the mound is...</i>

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:18.060
She's Wataru's twin sister.

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:22.800
Mayumura Michiru.

00:01:54.580 --> 00:01:56.300
What? No way!

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:59.930
The Mayumura 
Siblings

00:01:56.500 --> 00:01:59.930
The Dolphins actually 
made it to the quarterfinals?

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:03.260
Amazing, right? Aren't you impressed?!

00:02:03.680 --> 00:02:07.080
Now that <i>this</i> Shigeno Junior is on the team,

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:10.950
the once weak Dolphin Army has 
morphed into a baseball powerhouse!

00:02:11.490 --> 00:02:13.110
Wow, that's awesome!

00:02:13.110 --> 00:02:16.900
So did Hikaru-kun hit some
home runs and pitch shutouts?

00:02:17.850 --> 00:02:20.220
How did you figure that out?

00:02:20.780 --> 00:02:22.250
It was obvious.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:25.490
You guys made it to the third round,
where the matches get a lot harder.

00:02:25.730 --> 00:02:29.080
Which means there's no way 
you contributed much.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:30.690
How dare you!

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:32.720
I'll show you how much I've improved!

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.000
Let's take this outside!

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.020
Yawn.

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:38.540
No way. I'm too tired from 
pitching a whole game.

00:02:38.540 --> 00:02:39.750
You can't back out now!

00:02:39.750 --> 00:02:42.480
I'll show you my 
super-special sacrifice bunt!

00:02:42.480 --> 00:02:43.720
Huh? Your what?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:46.840
Daigo!

00:02:47.310 --> 00:02:51.160
How many times have I told you not 
to wear those filthy socks in the house?!

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.520
Get it through your head!

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:58.220
Put them in the washing machine 
and go take a shower already!

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:00.740
Aye aye, sir...

00:03:00.990 --> 00:03:02.730
Jeez, that kid...

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:05.010
Looks like the Dolphins won their games.

00:03:05.010 --> 00:03:07.890
Did he contribute to their victories at all?

00:03:07.890 --> 00:03:08.980
"Contribute"?

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.750
What are you talking about?

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:15.070
He's been playing a lot better than you think.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:16.060
Really?

00:03:23.740 --> 00:03:25.260
Huh? Mayumura?

00:03:25.730 --> 00:03:28.180
You mean, <i>that</i> Mayumura?

00:03:28.180 --> 00:03:29.350
That's right, Daigo.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:34.480
Mifune Dolphins

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:34.480
Coach  Fujii

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:34.480
Mifune Dolphins

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:34.480
Manager  Tashiro

00:03:29.350 --> 00:03:31.530
The very same Mayumura Ken 
who played in the majors,

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:34.400
just like your pop and Satou's father.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.830
There were a lot of amazing players 
in the same grade as Mayumura,

00:03:37.830 --> 00:03:41.190
and they earned themselves the nickname,
"Mayumura's Golden Generation."

00:03:41.190 --> 00:03:44.820
By the way, Tashiro and I
were also in the same grade.

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:48.860
Really? So you two were part 
of that golden generation?

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.250
Satou Hikaru

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.250
Ariyoshi

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:50.250
Matsubara

00:03:48.860 --> 00:03:50.060
You moron.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:54.540
Amateur players who happened to play in
the same era don't fall into that category.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:58.000
I'm not letting that slide.

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.010
Kimura

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.010
Kishimoto

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:03.010
Katsumata

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:03.010
I'll have you know, we battled Mayumura
to see which of us would get to Nationals.

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:07.510
Sakura Mutsuko

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.480
And we gave them a pretty 
good run for their money!

00:04:05.480 --> 00:04:07.510
The two of us and Shigeno Goro!

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:13.270
A-And his twins are
the Touto Boys' ace battery now?

00:04:13.270 --> 00:04:14.430
Looks that way.

00:04:14.430 --> 00:04:17.740
I didn't know Mayumura's kids 
played for the Touto Boys...

00:04:17.740 --> 00:04:20.230
until Urabe told me.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:24.410
Urabe Hayato

00:04:20.660 --> 00:04:25.850
Even I didn't know his sister
had become the ace, though.

00:04:27.060 --> 00:04:29.650
Back when Andy and I played
 for the Touto Boys,

00:04:29.650 --> 00:04:31.270
Michiru wanted to be an outfielder.

00:04:31.730 --> 00:04:36.080
It was her brother, Wataru, who wanted 
to be a pitcher, and he was my main rival.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:39.700
'Cause she's a girl, I never even 
considered Michiru a threat.

00:04:40.610 --> 00:04:45.690
I can't believe Wataru's now a catcher
and she's their pitcher.

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.070
Well, it's entirely possible he got injured.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:54.080
Either way, Touto has built 
the team around those two,

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.480
and they've shown that they're 
a force to be reckoned with.

00:04:57.480 --> 00:05:01.160
With the younger Mayumura playing cleanup,
their batting lineup is strong.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:03.240
Their defense is iron-tight, too.

00:05:04.350 --> 00:05:09.740
And then, there's their ace,
Mayumura Michiru, a lefty sidewinder.

00:05:11.210 --> 00:05:14.720
The speed of her pitches, their movement, 
and her control are all perfect.

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:16.740
I see no weaknesses in her game.

00:05:18.160 --> 00:05:22.050
We've fought hard to get to this point,
but they're a cut above.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.050
Let's chalk this up as a learning 
experience and give it all we've got.

00:05:27.780 --> 00:05:29.640
<i>That's what our manager said, but...</i>

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:35.430
<i>If we're gonna do this, I want to win.</i>

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.990
Touto Boys

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.990
Mayumura Michiru

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:50.090
Working out <i>again</i>, Michiru?

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.660
Touto Boys

00:05:53.120 --> 00:05:57.660
Mayumura Wataru

00:05:53.610 --> 00:05:57.830
Haven't we been told we're too young
to handle the stress of weight machines?

00:05:58.530 --> 00:06:02.130
Don't start doing things like this 
just 'cause Dad's away right now.

00:06:02.590 --> 00:06:03.420
I'll rat you out.

00:06:04.940 --> 00:06:09.770
Then, maybe I should go tell Mom that 
you've been using her expensive shampoo.

00:06:09.770 --> 00:06:11.150
H-How do you know that?!

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:14.890
W-Well, anyway,
let's talk about our next game.

00:06:15.130 --> 00:06:16.470
The Dolphins?

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:19.140
I don't think we need intel on <i>them</i>.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.670
Any team that makes it to the 
quarterfinals is there for a reason.

00:06:24.920 --> 00:06:25.530
Theirs is him.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:30.010
Satou Hikaru.

00:06:30.610 --> 00:06:34.210
From what I've heard, 
he's only just taken up baseball,

00:06:34.210 --> 00:06:36.190
and he's only their number two pitcher.

00:06:36.190 --> 00:06:38.750
But it looks like his pitches are 
around the 120 kmph mark.

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.250
Oh?

00:06:40.440 --> 00:06:43.380
And I also have it on good authority...

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:46.510
that the kid wearing
 the mask is Shigeno Daigo.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:52.340
This battery's made up of the kids of 
former major league players. Just like ours.

00:06:53.700 --> 00:06:57.270
Y-You mean, they're the sons of 
Shigeno Goro and Satou Toshiya?

00:06:57.910 --> 00:06:59.660
That's neither here nor there.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.040
Anyway, I jotted down the data 
of every batter in the notebook,

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.230
so make sure you look at it.

00:07:05.230 --> 00:07:06.320
R-Right.

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:10.430
I don't know if the Dolphins will use 
Satou or Urabe as their starting pitcher,

00:07:10.850 --> 00:07:14.010
but we've got a number of ways 
to counter Satou if they go with him.

00:07:15.030 --> 00:07:18.510
Anyway, don't think "it's only
 Regionals" and take it easy.

00:07:18.890 --> 00:07:20.450
Do your homework.

00:07:20.450 --> 00:07:21.620
Okay.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:29.970
<i>I don't believe it.</i>

00:07:33.380 --> 00:07:39.280
<i>I can't get my head around the fact that
I'm going up against the son of Shigeno-san,</i>

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:41.230
<i>the pitcher I admire the most.</i>

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:47.860
Hello. Urabe residence.

00:07:49.890 --> 00:07:51.060
Hayato!

00:07:51.060 --> 00:07:53.320
Manager Tashiro's on the phone for you.

00:07:58.130 --> 00:07:59.120
Hello?

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:00.730
<i>Ah, Urabe?</i>

00:08:00.730 --> 00:08:02.080
<i>Sorry to call at this hour.</i>

00:08:03.050 --> 00:08:04.270
What's wrong?

00:08:04.270 --> 00:08:05.460
Did something happen?

00:08:06.400 --> 00:08:08.130
<i>I've been thinking things over.</i>

00:08:08.130 --> 00:08:10.300
<i>And I talked to Fujii about it, too...</i>

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:16.300
<i>Would you mind if we go with Satou
as the starting pitcher against Touto?</i>

00:08:17.310 --> 00:08:20.360
What?!

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.050
It's lunchtime. Too early in the day to
be looking like the world's about to end.

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:39.910
Suzuki Andy

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:35.610
If I had to guess why,

00:08:35.610 --> 00:08:39.370
I'd say it's because you're a former ace 
who's had his starting spot stolen by a rookie

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:40.450
for the upcoming big game.

00:08:40.690 --> 00:08:42.810
You really beat about the bush, dontcha?

00:08:43.270 --> 00:08:45.460
It sucks, but that's how it goes.

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:50.460
Manager thinks Satou's pitches 
might be more effective against Touto.

00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:55.400
If he starts to struggle, you'll have 
to take over, whether you want to or not.

00:08:56.560 --> 00:08:58.550
I'm on first base and batting fourth.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:00.790
You're out in left field and batting third.

00:09:01.520 --> 00:09:04.580
It doesn't change the fact 
that we're taking on Touto.

00:09:05.470 --> 00:09:07.540
"That's how it goes," huh?

00:09:09.680 --> 00:09:13.210
So you also think Satou's better than me?

00:09:14.230 --> 00:09:16.570
Of course you do. Not much I can do about it.

00:09:17.510 --> 00:09:18.960
Well, whatever.

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:23.700
My main rival, Mayumura, has let 
his sister take his spot as pitcher, too.

00:09:24.540 --> 00:09:27.330
I really don't care anymore.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:29.640
What?

00:09:29.640 --> 00:09:31.380
Hikaru-kun's the starting pitcher?

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:32.440
Yeah.

00:09:32.440 --> 00:09:34.970
I got a call from Manager Tashiro about it.

00:09:35.310 --> 00:09:39.470
He said Hikaru would be our starting pitcher
for our quarterfinal game against Touto.

00:09:39.470 --> 00:09:41.320
Which means I'm playing catcher.

00:09:41.320 --> 00:09:42.240
Really?

00:09:42.240 --> 00:09:43.500
That's great!

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.460
Yup!

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:45.560
All right!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:49.340
I'll go to the cages after school and develop 
a strategy to take down the Mayumuras.

00:09:49.340 --> 00:09:50.000
Yeah!

00:09:50.000 --> 00:09:51.060
Let's do it!

00:09:51.060 --> 00:09:53.650
Wait, what? You're coming, too?

00:09:54.020 --> 00:09:56.200
Yeah, why? Got a problem with that?

00:09:56.610 --> 00:09:59.160
Mifune 
Batting Center

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:08.830
Fastballs

00:10:10.170 --> 00:10:11.190
It's no good.

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:12.940
What's wrong?

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.200
You got solid hits about half the time.

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:18.340
You didn't do too bad in there.

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.250
And that's the speed 
the girl in Touto pitches at.

00:10:22.680 --> 00:10:23.970
It's not good enough.

00:10:23.970 --> 00:10:26.060
According to Satou-san,

00:10:26.620 --> 00:10:31.720
if you don't get at least 20 hits
out of 25 on the machine,

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:34.820
you won't get a decent hit in a real game.

00:10:34.820 --> 00:10:36.070
Really?

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:45.330
Home 
Run

00:10:38.570 --> 00:10:45.330
Home 
Run

00:10:38.940 --> 00:10:41.850
The rhythm and the aim 
is always consistent on a machine,

00:10:41.850 --> 00:10:45.330
so if you can't hit them 100 percent 
of the time, you've got no hope in a game.

00:10:45.880 --> 00:10:50.820
And she's also a left-handed sidewinder. 
She throws a pitch we've never seen before.

00:10:51.370 --> 00:10:55.820
I can hit all the balls I want here, 
but I don't know if it'll help any.

00:10:55.820 --> 00:10:58.170
Well, it's better than 
sitting around, doing nothing.

00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:03.040
Hikaru-kun can't get here on weekdays, 
so you can't practice catching, anyway.

00:11:15.550 --> 00:11:16.330
<i>Who's that?</i>

00:11:16.330 --> 00:11:18.860
<i>Their hits sound really good.</i>

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.860
Fastballs

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.860
For both batting positions

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.860
Right-handed pitcher

00:11:22.320 --> 00:11:23.820
Home
Run

00:11:25.240 --> 00:11:26.450
<i>A girl?</i>

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:38.550
<i>Huh?! M-Muh-M-Mayumura Michiru!</i>

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:41.820
<i>Touto Boys' ace!</i>

00:11:53.270 --> 00:11:54.100
Hold it!

00:11:54.920 --> 00:11:58.480
Could you be Shigeno Daigo-kun?

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:02.150
U-Uh, yeah, I am.

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.640
I-It's so nice to meet you!

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:11.330
My name's Mayumura Michiru,
and I'm Touto Boys' pitcher!

00:12:15.190 --> 00:12:16.880
Your turn again, Shigeno-kun.

00:12:16.880 --> 00:12:17.620
Huh?

00:12:17.990 --> 00:12:19.450
Shigeno-kun?

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:27.970
S-Seriously?

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.830
Yeah, sure!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:32.230
I mean, that's what you 
want to practice, isn't it?

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:33.790
B-But...

00:12:35.190 --> 00:12:37.650
Reception

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:40.610
<i>I didn't realize he was here, too!</i>

00:12:41.050 --> 00:12:44.740
Well, well, if it isn't the Dolphins' catcher.

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.030
We got talking just now.

00:12:47.550 --> 00:12:50.910
We're heading off to practice 
at Shigeno-kun's house.

00:12:52.900 --> 00:12:55.020
What are you talking about, Michiru?

00:12:55.020 --> 00:12:57.070
Don't be stupid. We're going home.

00:12:57.070 --> 00:13:00.210
I don't want to. You can go home by yourself.

00:13:01.900 --> 00:13:04.210
Wh-What's going on?!

00:13:04.210 --> 00:13:07.760
This is really weird. We're about 
to play them in a tournament.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:10.160
How did you end up in this crazy situation?

00:13:10.160 --> 00:13:12.510
I know how strange it sounds,

00:13:12.510 --> 00:13:16.560
but she said she'd let me practice 
hitting her sidearm pitch.

00:13:17.910 --> 00:13:20.660
I figured it was a great 
opportunity, so I said okay.

00:13:22.000 --> 00:13:24.820
<i>Don't tell me Michiru's...</i>

00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.020
Let's go, then.

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:27.990
Shi-ge-no-kun!

00:13:27.990 --> 00:13:29.380
R-Right...

00:13:29.940 --> 00:13:33.240
"Sh-Shi-ge-no-kun"?!

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:46.300
Resignation

00:13:48.330 --> 00:13:50.640
So this is your house, huh?

00:13:50.890 --> 00:13:53.700
Wow! You even having a batting cage.

00:13:53.700 --> 00:13:57.460
Y-Yeah. My older sister plays baseball, too.

00:13:57.460 --> 00:13:59.540
Oh, really?

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.630
Yeah. So should we start off 
with a game of catch?

00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:04.030
Ah, sorry, but...

00:14:04.650 --> 00:14:06.890
I'm dying for a drink.

00:14:06.890 --> 00:14:09.410
Would it be okay if I got a glass of water?

00:14:09.410 --> 00:14:10.970
Uh, sure.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.500
Here. Barley tea okay?

00:14:16.500 --> 00:14:18.680
Oh, yes, thank you.

00:14:22.730 --> 00:14:23.590
What's that?

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.480
<i>Oh, crap! That's...</i>

00:14:29.050 --> 00:14:32.330
Y-You know, we should really 
get started once we've drunk this.

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:33.710
Or the sun will set before...

00:14:37.680 --> 00:14:38.760
Oh, wow!

00:14:38.770 --> 00:14:41.230
Shigeno 
Goro

00:14:38.950 --> 00:14:41.230
It's Shigeno Goro!

00:14:42.610 --> 00:14:45.530
Does that mean he's your dad?

00:14:45.530 --> 00:14:46.610
U-Uh, yeah.

00:14:47.460 --> 00:14:49.110
<i>The cat's out of the bag now...</i>

00:14:49.110 --> 00:14:52.370
Oh, wow, that's amazing!

00:14:53.540 --> 00:14:55.950
Oh, that plaque there is the Cy Young Award!

00:14:56.670 --> 00:14:59.860
And that's a World Series ring!

00:15:02.160 --> 00:15:08.450
Though, if my dad hadn't lost that game, 
this ring would be in our house right now.

00:15:08.900 --> 00:15:10.630
Uh, sorry about that.

00:15:10.630 --> 00:15:12.930
Oh, I didn't mean it like that.

00:15:12.930 --> 00:15:15.270
I don't believe that guy!

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:17.070
What an idiot!

00:15:17.070 --> 00:15:19.420
How could he just ditch me 
at the batting center,

00:15:19.420 --> 00:15:22.190
and take a female adversary 
back to his house?!

00:15:23.430 --> 00:15:28.420
So Shigeno-kun, did you start playing
because you looked up to your dad?

00:15:28.870 --> 00:15:30.150
Uh, yeah.

00:15:30.370 --> 00:15:33.100
So why didn't you try becoming a pitcher?

00:15:33.100 --> 00:15:35.740
Don't you play catcher for your team?

00:15:36.350 --> 00:15:37.150
Yeah.

00:15:37.150 --> 00:15:39.080
I don't have a very strong arm.

00:15:39.340 --> 00:15:40.460
That's all?

00:15:40.460 --> 00:15:41.210
What?

00:15:41.890 --> 00:15:44.420
That's enough to make you 
stop wanting to be a pitcher?

00:15:44.420 --> 00:15:48.800
Sounds like you haven't tried very hard 
to follow in your dad's footsteps.

00:15:49.010 --> 00:15:51.050
Th-That's not true...

00:15:51.330 --> 00:15:53.180
I think it is.

00:15:54.200 --> 00:15:58.350
I reckon I look up to 
Shigeno Goro more than you do.

00:16:02.300 --> 00:16:03.630
Whoops, sorry about that.

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:05.440
I kinda did a real throw that time.

00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:06.810
So this is his place.

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:07.400
Huh?

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:08.830
Sorry.

00:16:08.830 --> 00:16:11.370
I didn't know where he lived, 
so I just followed you.

00:16:11.930 --> 00:16:13.520
I'm coming in, Shigeno.

00:16:14.890 --> 00:16:16.910
What are you doing, Michiru?

00:16:17.550 --> 00:16:20.600
Stop getting so buddy-buddy with 
our opponents before the big game.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:21.910
Time to leave.

00:16:21.910 --> 00:16:23.530
You're so annoying.

00:16:23.530 --> 00:16:24.960
I mean, what's the problem?

00:16:25.280 --> 00:16:28.120
We're just two kids of pro players, 
getting to know each other.

00:16:28.120 --> 00:16:31.670
Your motive is clear for all to see.

00:16:32.070 --> 00:16:35.180
You're trying to suck up 
to your favorite player's son...

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:38.520
in the hope that he'll introduce 
you to his dad one day.

00:16:40.800 --> 00:16:43.700
Why do you have to expose me like that?

00:16:43.700 --> 00:16:45.190
You're so obnoxious.

00:16:45.400 --> 00:16:46.930
Did you hear that?

00:16:46.930 --> 00:16:51.020
She only approached you because 
she hero-worships your father.

00:16:51.020 --> 00:16:52.570
How rude is <i>that</i>?!

00:16:52.570 --> 00:16:54.680
It's okay, really.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:57.780
I thought it was a little 
too good to be true,

00:16:58.390 --> 00:17:01.430
but I don't mind as long as 
I get to see her pitches.

00:17:01.430 --> 00:17:04.080
Let me practice with the real deal already.

00:17:05.360 --> 00:17:09.290
If you're really such a huge fan of my pop, 
I'll introduce you to him when he's back.

00:17:09.290 --> 00:17:09.870
What?

00:17:09.870 --> 00:17:11.130
R-Really?!

00:17:12.630 --> 00:17:13.810
Stop messing around!

00:17:13.810 --> 00:17:15.060
We're going home <i>now</i>, Michiru!

00:17:15.710 --> 00:17:20.310
Now, look here! Instead of 
complaining, put on your mask.

00:17:20.310 --> 00:17:21.470
What?

00:17:22.190 --> 00:17:23.780
What are you so scared about?

00:17:23.780 --> 00:17:26.900
Even if he sees my pitch, 
it's not like he'll be able to hit it,

00:17:26.900 --> 00:17:28.940
and he'll just give up 
after a couple of throws.

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:33.920
All right, here we go!

00:17:39.910 --> 00:17:41.130
Strike.

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:44.290
Amazing!

00:17:44.530 --> 00:17:49.090
<i>Yikes. That really angled in from the right.</i>

00:17:52.770 --> 00:17:54.010
That was in the strike zone.

00:17:57.130 --> 00:17:59.190
<i>No way! She's so cool!</i>

00:17:59.190 --> 00:18:01.350
<i>I saw her do that before, 
but from really far away.</i>

00:18:04.580 --> 00:18:08.690
<i>Girls can throw such amazing pitches, too!</i>

00:18:09.100 --> 00:18:10.430
All right, good hustle.

00:18:10.430 --> 00:18:11.160
What?

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:13.210
You're satisfied now, aren't you?

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:16.860
You won't be able to hit 
Michiru's pitches with <i>your</i> swing.

00:18:17.310 --> 00:18:18.230
See ya.

00:18:19.330 --> 00:18:21.300
H-H-Hang on!

00:18:22.350 --> 00:18:24.680
You're jumping the gun way too soon.

00:18:24.680 --> 00:18:27.280
That was only three pitches!

00:18:27.670 --> 00:18:30.810
Sheesh. Looks like you 
don't know when to give up.

00:18:30.810 --> 00:18:32.010
Oh, I know!

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:35.990
If you throw me some more balls, 
I'll get my pop to sign a ball for you.

00:18:35.990 --> 00:18:37.510
Huh? You mean it?

00:18:37.800 --> 00:18:38.590
Yeah!

00:18:38.590 --> 00:18:40.230
I'll do it! I'll throw more!

00:18:40.230 --> 00:18:42.460
H-Hey! Michiru!

00:18:46.680 --> 00:18:48.660
Mom, can I borrow your phone a sec?

00:18:48.660 --> 00:18:50.860
Sure, but what do you need it for?

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:52.550
To call Pop.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:55.520
I want to ask him something.

00:18:59.220 --> 00:19:00.200
<i>Hey, hey!</i>

00:19:00.200 --> 00:19:02.780
Hey, Pop! It's me.

00:19:02.780 --> 00:19:04.110
<i>Hey, Daigo!</i>

00:19:04.110 --> 00:19:04.990
<i>How are you doing?</i>

00:19:05.570 --> 00:19:11.160
<i>Oh, your mother told me the Dolphins 
made it to the quarterfinals.</i>

00:19:11.160 --> 00:19:16.310
Yeah, our next opponent's the 
team Mayumura's twins play for.

00:19:16.310 --> 00:19:18.400
<i>Yeah? Mayumura's twins, huh?</i>

00:19:18.400 --> 00:19:22.260
Yeah. They're a battery. The sister 
pitches and the brother catches.

00:19:22.760 --> 00:19:25.670
The girl told me she's your biggest fan.

00:19:26.350 --> 00:19:27.280
<i>She's a fan?</i>

00:19:27.280 --> 00:19:29.270
<i>She'll definitely make it big, then.</i>

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:33.270
To be honest, she's an 
amazing pitcher already.

00:19:33.270 --> 00:19:36.020
Their batting lineup is also really strong.

00:19:36.180 --> 00:19:38.190
<i>So it looks like it's going
 to be a tough game, huh?</i>

00:19:38.190 --> 00:19:40.020
Yeah. Really tough.

00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:42.160
But I really want to win!

00:19:42.160 --> 00:19:44.350
Which is why I wanted to ask 
your advice on something.

00:19:44.350 --> 00:19:44.980
<i>Oh?</i>

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:46.360
<i>Ask me anything.</i>

00:19:46.360 --> 00:19:47.380
The other day,

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:50.920
Hikaru said he'd like to know if there 
was a trick to improving his control.

00:19:50.920 --> 00:19:53.050
Got any advice for him?

00:19:54.370 --> 00:19:55.790
<i>Well, uh...</i>

00:20:01.120 --> 00:20:03.250
What's wrong with you?

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:07.480
Surely you're not still depressed...

00:20:07.480 --> 00:20:10.540
A little. But that's not all.

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:16.520
Yesterday, Mayumura-san threw 20 to 30 
pitches for me till the sun went down.

00:20:17.310 --> 00:20:22.100
But I only managed to graze 
a few of them right at the end.

00:20:23.720 --> 00:20:28.180
I thought, maybe if she threw more at me,
 I could figure out how to hit them,

00:20:28.180 --> 00:20:29.980
but that wasn't the case.

00:20:29.980 --> 00:20:31.510
It's not your fault.

00:20:31.510 --> 00:20:33.370
Mayumura-san's something else.

00:20:34.440 --> 00:20:38.560
I mean, she's just the coolest, isn't she?

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:42.360
She mows down the hordes of boys 
who step up to the plate in front of her.

00:20:42.360 --> 00:20:43.590
That's like, goals!

00:20:44.130 --> 00:20:45.840
That's what you're admiring?

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:51.360
Anyway, it's clear now that someone at
my level hasn't got a hope against her.

00:20:51.800 --> 00:20:54.260
So what are you saying? You're giving up?

00:20:54.260 --> 00:20:57.780
No. I can't hit my way out, but I <i>can</i>
come up with a strategy to counter her.

00:20:58.680 --> 00:20:59.690
Bunts.

00:21:00.140 --> 00:21:04.450
Mastering bunts is my only hope 
if I want to get on base.

00:21:04.870 --> 00:21:06.330
"Mastering"?

00:21:06.330 --> 00:21:07.070
Yes.

00:21:08.100 --> 00:21:09.790
To practice those, though,

00:21:09.790 --> 00:21:13.250
I need a pitcher who has 
both speed and control.

00:21:13.640 --> 00:21:16.010
Are you talking about...

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:19.000
Mifune City
Higashibara
Elementary School

00:21:19.250 --> 00:21:20.960
Oh, there he is!

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:23.420
Hey, Urabe-kun!

00:21:23.850 --> 00:21:24.780
Huh?

00:21:24.780 --> 00:21:28.470
Why have you guys come 
all the way to my school?

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:29.760
Sorry.

00:21:29.760 --> 00:21:31.850
Actually, we wanted to ask you a favor.

00:21:32.040 --> 00:21:33.390
A favor?

00:21:33.390 --> 00:21:35.940
If this favor concerns baseball,
you can forget it.

00:21:36.140 --> 00:21:36.970
Huh?

00:21:38.680 --> 00:21:39.940
H-Hey!

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.390
At least hear me out!

00:21:42.390 --> 00:21:45.130
I want to practice bunting!

00:21:46.400 --> 00:21:48.540
And not the sacrifice bunts I usually do,

00:21:48.540 --> 00:21:52.540
but bunting for a base hit 
so I can get on base for you guys, too.

00:21:53.560 --> 00:21:57.420
That's the only chance I'll be able to create
against Mayumura Michiru's pitches.

00:21:58.340 --> 00:22:01.090
That's why I want you as my 
batting practice pitcher, Urabe.

00:22:01.570 --> 00:22:05.340
Hikaru's in Gunma, and 
there's no one else I can ask.

00:22:06.580 --> 00:22:07.970
Me? A batting practice pitcher?!

00:22:08.550 --> 00:22:10.010
Who do you think you are?!

00:22:10.880 --> 00:22:14.930
I'm a second-string pitcher now, so you
think it's fine to ask me that? Is that it?

00:22:16.500 --> 00:22:19.190
How far I've fallen, huh?

00:22:19.720 --> 00:22:21.190
This is so dumb.

00:22:21.190 --> 00:22:22.850
Do what you like!

00:22:22.850 --> 00:22:26.070
I'm quitting the Dolphins, anyway, 
so it's none of my business anymore!

00:22:26.070 --> 00:22:30.030
Resignation

00:24:01.400 --> 00:24:03.540
Urabe's quitting the Dolphins?

00:24:03.910 --> 00:24:08.000
I mean, I get how he feels, 
but he can't do this!

00:24:08.190 --> 00:24:10.170
We got this far as a team!

00:24:10.590 --> 00:24:14.170
We need to win the next match 
together, as the Dolphins!

00:24:14.170 --> 00:24:17.750
I promise I'll master 
bunting for a base hit, too!

00:24:18.060 --> 00:24:25.020
Before the Big Game

00:24:18.500 --> 00:24:21.060
Next time: "Before the Big Game."

00:24:21.060 --> 00:24:23.180
Run to the stage of your dreams!
